{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24771 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "Haliclorensin B is implicated in the regulation of CD70 antigen through a series of molecular interactions involving the vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1. This subunit serves as a target for Haliclorensin B, which in turn influences the activity of other compounds such as Spruceanol and Capensinidin. These latter compounds also target CD70 antigen, suggesting a potential pathway where Haliclorensin B modulates the expression or function of CD70 antigen via the vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1. The evidence indicates that Haliclorensin B may act as a modulator of CD70 antigen through a shared target, highlighting a possible regulatory mechanism involving the vacuolar ATP synthase. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1 as a central mediator in the relationship between Haliclorensin B and CD70 antigen.",
